.Dd July 7, 2026
.Dt JC 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm jc
.Nd provision a jj repository and its workspaces from a config file
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads a UCL-formatted configuration file and provisions a local
dev workspace managed by
.Xr jj 1 .
From a single config file it initializes a colocated jj repository,
registers the configured git remotes, fetches from them, tracks the
configured bookmarks, creates one jj workspace per configured
workspace, and applies repository-local jj configuration.
.Pp
.Nm
is run in the dev workspace: the directory that holds
.Pa jc.conf .
Each configured workspace is created as a subdirectory of it named
.Ar name Ns .jj .
The workspace named
.Dq default
is jj's initial workspace and holds the repository store; each
additional workspace is a linked jj workspace sharing that repository.
The default workspace is colocated with git, so standard git tools
work directly in it; linked workspaces are managed by jj alone.
.Pp
.Nm
is idempotent.
Running it again against an already-provisioned dev workspace
reconciles it with the config: missing remotes, workspaces, and
configuration are added, and existing ones are left untouched.
Working copies are positioned only when a workspace is first created;
reconciling never moves them.
It never discards local work.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
The configuration file is UCL.
It recognizes the following top-level keys.
.Bl -tag -width push_repo
.It Cm remotes
An array of git remotes to register on the repository.
Each element is an object with the keys:
.Bl -tag -width bookmark
.It Cm name
The local name of the remote.
.It Cm src
The git URL fetched from and, unless overridden, pushed to.
.El
.It Cm workspaces
An array of workspaces to create.
One workspace must be named
.Dq default .
Each element is an object with the keys:
.Bl -tag -width bookmark
.It Cm name
The jj workspace name.
The workspace is created in the subdirectory
.Ar name Ns .jj .
.It Cm bookmark
Optional.
The bookmark the workspace is based on.
.It Cm remote
Optional.
The remote the bookmark is tracked from.
When
.Cm bookmark
and
.Cm remote
are given, the bookmark is tracked and the workspace working copy is
placed on a new change atop the tracked remote bookmark.
The working copy is never placed on an immutable commit directly.
When
.Cm bookmark
is omitted and a bookmark matching the workspace name exists, the
workspace is based on that bookmark; otherwise it is created with
.Xr jj 1 Ns 's
default base for new workspaces.
.El
.It Cm push_repo
Optional.
The
.Cm name
of the remote that bookmarks are pushed to by default.
It must name a remote from
.Cm remotes .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width jc.conf
.It Pa jc.conf
Configuration file, read from the current directory.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Given
.Pa jc.conf :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
remotes = [
  {name: "upstream", src: "https://github.com/allanjude/uclcmd.git"},
  {name: "gh-pm", src: "git@github.com:patmaddox/uclcmd.git"}
]

workspaces = [
  {name: "default", bookmark: "master", remote: "upstream"},
  {name: "man-page"}
]

push_repo = "gh-pm"
.Ed
.Pp
running
.Nm
in the directory holding it produces:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
\&./default.jj/     workspace on a new change atop master@upstream
\&./man-page.jj/    workspace on jj's default base
.Ed
.Pp
with the
.Va upstream
and
.Va gh-pm
remotes registered and fetched, the
.Va master
bookmark tracking
.Va master@upstream ,
and bookmarks pushed to
.Va gh-pm
by default.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jj 1
